# PAM configuration file for Cyrus POP3 service.
#
# This file is sourced by Cyrus SASL for authentication and account
# management when using PAM as the backend. It allows overriding
# the standard Debian/Ubuntu PAM stack names for auth and account
# checks, enabling custom PAM hierarchies or remote authentication
# sources.
#
# IMPORTANT: If Cyrus is used in a setup where users do not have
# local system accounts, ensure you use something like `pam_permit`
# or a dedicated auth module for account checking to avoid
# authentication failures due to missing local users.
#
# Note: SASL (and therefore Cyrus) accesses PAM modules through
# saslauthd. SASL can only handle plaintext passwords if PAM is
# used; other methods (e.g., OTP, Kerberos) may require different
# configurations.

# PAM include directive for authentication.
# Specifies the PAM configuration file fragment to use for
# authenticating users against the Cyrus POP3 service.
# Default: 'common-auth' (standard Debian/Ubuntu auth stack).
# Example: 'common-auth' or '/etc/pam.d/custom-auth'
@include {{ common_auth_include | default('common-auth') }}

# PAM include directive for account management.
# Specifies the PAM configuration file fragment to use for
# checking account status (expiration, access controls) for
# users on the Cyrus POP3 service.
# Default: 'common-account' (standard Debian/Ubuntu account stack).
# Example: 'common-account' or '/etc/pam.d/custom-account'
@include {{ common_account_include | default('common-account') }}